# KSI-CNA-RNT / KSI-SVC-SNT / KSI-CNA-DFP: Network Traffic Restriction
# Validates that an EC2 workload's security group enforces least-privilege
# network access. The specific ports below are an example deployment
# (HTTPS frontend + application TLS + control-plane gRPC); substitute
# your own ports for your workload.
# - Ingress: only ports 443, 3443, 50051 from VPC CIDR
# - No ingress from 0.0.0.0/0
# - Egress: only 443, 80, 53
# - No ingress from anywhere boolean = false (VPC-scoped rules only)

META
    esp_id `ksi-cna-rnt-svc-snt-network-restriction-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `aws`
    criticality `critical`

    title `KSI-CNA-RNT / KSI-SVC-SNT / KSI-CNA-DFP: Network Traffic Restriction`
    description `Validates the workload VM security group restricts ingress to required ports from VPC CIDR only with no open internet access`
    author `example-security`
    tags `aws,security-group,network,ingress,egress,fedramp,KSI-CNA-RNT,KSI-SVC-SNT,KSI-CNA-DFP`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CNA-RNT,KSI:KSI-SVC-SNT,KSI:KSI-CNA-DFP`
    control_objective `KSI-CNA-RNT,KSI-SVC-SNT,KSI-CNA-DFP`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `AWS:us-east-1:compute-infrastructure`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Ensure the VM security group has no 0.0.0.0/0 ingress rules. Restrict ingress to ports 443, 3443, and 50051 from the VPC CIDR only.`

    component_id `comp-aws-compute`

    impl_KSI_CNA_RNT `Network traffic restriction is validated by confirming the workload VM security group (example-org-vm-sg) has no ingress rules allowing traffic from 0.0.0.0/0 (has_ingress_from_anywhere = false). The ingress rule count is validated to confirm only the three required ports are open: 443 (HTTPS frontend), 3443 (application TLS), and 50051 (control-plane gRPC). All ingress is scoped to the VPC CIDR, ensuring no direct internet inbound path exists to the instance.`

    impl_KSI_SVC_SNT `Network traffic security is validated by confirming ingress is restricted to TLS-capable ports only (443, 3443) and the gRPC port (50051), all sourced from the VPC CIDR. Egress is limited to ports 443 (HTTPS), 80 (HTTP for package mirrors), and 53 (DNS). The instance has no public IP (validated separately in the instance hardening policy), ensuring all traffic traverses the VPC boundary without direct internet exposure.`

    impl_KSI_CNA_DFP `Functionality and privilege definition at the network layer is validated by confirming the security group enforces exactly the ports required for the workload: port 443 for HTTPS dashboard and API, port 3443 for mTLS daemon communication, and port 50051 for gRPC control-plane connectivity. The ingress_rule_count = 3 confirms no additional unauthorized ports have been opened beyond the documented baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    VAR aws_region string `us-east-1`
    VAR vm_sg_id string `sg-0123456789abcdef1`
    VAR vpc_id string `vpc-0123456789abcdef0`

    OBJECT vm_security_group
        group_id VAR vm_sg_id
        region VAR aws_region
    OBJECT_END

    # VM SG: no open ingress, exactly 3 ingress rules (443, 3443, 50051)
    STATE vm_sg_compliant
        found boolean = true
        vpc_id string = VAR vpc_id
        has_ingress_from_anywhere boolean = false
        ingress_rule_count int = 3
        record
            field IpPermissions.*.FromPort int = 443 at_least_one
            field IpPermissions.*.FromPort int = 3443 at_least_one
            field IpPermissions.*.FromPort int = 50051 at_least_one
        record_end
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN aws_security_group
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF vm_sg_compliant
            OBJECT_REF vm_security_group
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
